@prn

@buruh

Though electorally small, allying the smaller parties like the <span style="color: #FF6666;">**PSI**</span> or the <span style="color: #FF9933;">**PIR**</span> can be crucial in forming cabinet coalitions.

@islam

- @masyumi_ties: Meet with their leadership to develop closer ties with the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span>.
- @sukiman_connections: Sukiman, the head of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span> legislative branch, is more in line with our current leadership. Perhaps we can establish connections with him?
- @sukiman_connections1: The older generation of leaders, men like Sidik and Sartono, are seen as more cooperative than other <span style="color: #990000;">**PNI**</span> leaders by the current <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span> leadership. Perhaps we can use them to appease the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span>? 
- @natsir_connections: The younger, more moderate leaders, such as Wilopo, are seen as more cooperative than other <span style="color: #990000;">**PNI**</span> leaders by the current <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span> leadership. Perhaps we can use Wilopo to appease the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span>? 
- @interparty: What about the other parties?

@masyumi_ties
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: masyumi_op if not pni_in_government and masyumi_in_government; masyumi_1 if pni_in_government and masyumi_in_government

@masyumi_op
on-arrival: masyumi_relation += 2*(wilopo_strength / 10); 

We are currently in opposition to the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span> and our relations remain cold. However this may change.

@masyumi_1
on-arrival: masyumi_relation += 4*(wilopo_strength / 10); 

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@sukiman_connections
subtitle: -1 resources
view-if: (((sidik_strength > wilopo_strength) and (sidik_strength > partindo_strength)) or ((partindo_strength > wilopo_strength) and (partindo_strength > sidik_strength))) and masyumi_leader == "Muhammad Natsir"
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; masyumi_relation += 4*(wilopo_strength / 10);

@sukiman_connections1
subtitle: -1 resources
view-if: (wilopo_strength > sidik_strength) and (wilopo_strength > partindo_strength) and masyumi_leader == "Soekiman Wirjosandjojo"
choose-if: resources >= 1 and partindo_dissent <= 20 and sidik_dissent <= 20
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources <= 1: Not enough resources. ?][? if partindo_dissent >= 20 or sidik_dissent >= 20: The party is unwilling. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 1; partindo_strength += 2; sidik_dissent += 2

@natsir_connections
subtitle: -1 resources
view-if: (((sidik_strength > wilopo_strength) and (sidik_strength > partindo_strength)) or ((partindo_strength > wilopo_strength) and (partindo_strength > sidik_strength))) and masyumi_leader == "Muhammad Natsir"
choose-if: resources >= 1 and wilopo_dissent <= 20
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources <= 1: Not enough resources. ?][? if wilopo_dissent >= 20: The party is unwilling. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 1; wilopo_strength += 3

@nasrani
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; kristen_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); 

Representing religious minorities, these parties can be reliable partners in regional matters.

@pni_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

